  "question": {
    "text": "Effective capacitance of parallel combination of two capacitors <math><msub><mrow><mi>C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi>C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> is <math><mn>10</mn><mi></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mo>.</mo></math> When these capacitors are individually connected to a voltage source of <math><mn>1</mn><mi></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>,</mo></math> the energy stored in the capacitor <math><msub><mrow><mi>C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> is <math><mn>4</mn></math> times that of <math><msub><mrow><mi>C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>.</mo></math> If these capacitors are connected in series, their effective capacitance will be:"
  },
